This skill adapts ideas and condensed prompt wording from:
- TauricResearch/TradingAgents (Apache-2.0)
- HKUDS/Vibe-Trading, virattt/ai-hedge-fund, Jakeschincariol/day-trader-skill,
  alpacahq/alpaca-mcp-server, ZhuLinsen/daily_stock_analysis, LosaLosSantos/aurelio-finance,
  mvanhorn/last30days-skill, shiyu-coder/Kronos, janestreet/agent_skills (MIT)
- OpenBB, OpenByteInc/QuantDinger, goldmansachs/gs-quant, zipline-reloaded (Apache-2.0)
- polars (MIT); pyfolio-reloaded, solders (Apache-2.0); backtesting.py (AGPL-3.0, referenced as a dependency only)
- @DN_degen, "I Was Asleep. My AI Desk Wasn't" (X article, 2026-11-15): kill-filter and desk structure, paraphrased
- NautilusTrader (LGPL-3.0), PyBroker (Apache-2.0 + Commons Clause), vectorbt (Fair-code), HftBacktest (MIT): referenced as external dependencies only
- roan-maverick/MIT-trader-skill (MIT): rule-screening method, reimplemented in scripts/rule_screen.py; its CC BY-NC-SA lecture notes are linked, not included
- Permutation gates in scripts/permutation_test.py: original code following Timothy Masters' permutation-testing method as described in a @rohonchain article (2026-11-11)
- Black-Litterman (Black & Litterman 1992; confidence-scaled Omega in the spirit of Idzorek 2005): original code in scripts/black_litterman.py. Prompted by aardisaputra/uchicago_case3, which has no license, so none of its code is used
- Event-timing gate thresholds in scripts/risk_check.py: ideas from udiedrichsen/stock-analysis (openclaw skill); original code
- Crash-protection rules in scripts/crash_guard.py: original code following hft.md/crash (vol targeting, drawdown brake, trend filter, risk contribution, stress test; S&P 500 crash levels as published there)
- Capability list for v1.7 (scorecard, filings watch, options, prediction markets, rebalancing, journals, briefs): ideas from the hft.md Grok Bot directory and cs68614-hash/awesome-grokbot-templates (CC0); no bot prompts were available or used
- MCP servers referenced, not bundled: stefanoamorelli/sec-edgar-mcp (AGPL-3.0), JamesANZ/prediction-market-mcp (MIT)
- freqtrade (GPL-3.0): referenced via its CLI only; no freqtrade code is included.
No code from these projects is copied except short illustrative API examples.
